      "english": "Freud viewed dreams as disguised wish-fulfillments of repressed unconscious desires, and anger was no exception. Anger suppressed by the waking ego and superego undergoes 'dream-work' — through displacement, condensation, and symbolism — and surfaces in a transformed form during sleep. A common pattern Freud described is transferring anger toward authority figures (bosses, parents) onto a safer, more neutral dream character. Freud noted that emotional content in dreams — including anger — tends to be genuine and undisguised, even when the people or objects it is directed at are symbolic stand-ins."
